# Shared dev/e2e defaults, matching what .github/workflows/pages.yml sets
# for CI builds. Not secrets:
# - VITE_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID is functionally unused by the proxy, which
#   injects the real GITHUB_CLIENT_ID server-side regardless of what's sent
#   here — required only because @octokit/auth-oauth-device needs a
#   non-empty clientId to construct its requests.
# - VITE_SYNCED_SHARE_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID is the *separate*, dedicated
#   GitHub OAuth App used only for Synced Share's identity sign-in (see
#   `useSyncedShareOwner.ts` and `syncedShareGithubAuth.ts`). Deliberately a
#   different app/client id from VITE_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID above -- sharing
#   one app meant GitHub's consent screen for this identity-only sign-in
#   showed the storage app's full `repo` grant as "existing access", which
#   defeated the point of keeping it minimally-scoped. Real (not a
#   placeholder) because, unlike the storage flow, this one sends it
#   directly to GitHub's authorization endpoint from the browser.
# - VITE_SYNCED_SHARE_HOST is exposed client-side regardless of where it's set.
# Override locally via the gitignored .env.local if needed.
VITE_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=placeholder-client-id
VITE_SYNCED_SHARE_GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=Ov23liFN0gIJmZ2VREGm
VITE_GITHUB_OAUTH_PROXY_URL=https://jianpu-oauth-proxy.pages.dev
VITE_SYNCED_SHARE_HOST=jianpu-live-share-worker-rs.hou32hou.workers.dev
